From: eisen0419 <usetoken0419@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:32:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] library: billion-context uses the configured bili port when
 8787 is taken
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#7382, wxy0626. Enabling Zed, Hermes or dsh no longer probes a hardcoded
127.0.0.1:8787. The shared bili start uses ACP_PORT, then PORT, then
port in billion-context.json, otherwise 8787, and the health probe and
the /bili/ prefix use that same origin. A foreign listener on the default
8787 (a 401, not bili's health) is left alone; a bili already answering
from 18787 is used instead. A port the file sets is not replaced.

A 503 {"ok":false,"reason":"starting"} is bili itself, bound before
registration finishes, so the child is kept until health is ok. Health
probing separates TCP dialing (biliDialTimeout = 3s; any connect failure,
including Windows' ~2s loopback RST retry, is biliDown) from post-connect
HTTP replies (biliProbeTimeout = 2s + conn deadline; disconnect or stall
after TCP accept is biliStalled). Pre-spawn probes skip biliStalled and
biliOther on lane ports, while biliStartAt waits out biliStalled while our
own child stays alive rather than killing it as a port conflict.

BILI_CONFIG_FILE and XDG_CONFIG_HOME are read through appdir.LookupEnv /
appdir.Getenv so rooted XDG paths, Windows registry updates, relative
BILI_CONFIG_FILE paths and bare named configs work cleanly. Blank
whitespace-only BILI_CONFIG_FILE is treated as unset rather than flagging
a missing named config (matching checkNamedConfigRef), and unreadable or
malformed config files fall back to default 8787 (matching loadConfigFile).
An empty ACP_PORT or PORT is an error and does not fall through; JSON
null is 8787 and 8787.5 is 8787, as parseInt does.

Moving the daemon rewrites only the outer /bili/ prefix on magpie's own
provider entries in active URL-lane agents: Zed, Hermes (magpie,
magpie-anthropic) and dsh (following dshFiles: profile patch lists, home
patch and settings.yaml when profiles exist, else legacy config.yaml
llm-deepseek), leaving user-defined providers on other /bili/ ports and
YAML comments untouched. Alignment runs under biliMu, logs errors from
other active agents without failing the toggled agent's switch, backs up
each aligned agent's main file, and stops the started daemon if bili was
disabled while startup was in flight.

#7310 is the other side of that split. bili's Claude plugin writes the
lane port 18787 into ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, while bili start's user-zone
daemon is 8787 unless the file or the environment names another port.
This does not rewrite the URL bili's own plugin writes.

Verified:
- gofmt -l clean on all touched Go files
- go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestBili|Test.*Bili|TestAlignBili|TestKeepBili|TestMoveBili|TestSetBiliURL' ./internal/library/ ./internal/agent/ (PASS)
- go test -race -count=1 ./internal/appdir/ (PASS)
- go vet ./internal/library/ ./internal/agent/ ./internal/appdir/ (darwin, GOOS=linux -tags nogui, GOOS=windows — all clean)
- TestBiliUsesConfiguredPortWhen8787Answers401 fails without this change.
